WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Speaker 1: The Russian invasion of Ukraine&nbsp;
continues. And I want to get everybody up to speed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:09.600
there before we move on to other things. And as&nbsp;
always, when we say we have a report of something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.640
that's what we mean. We have a report of&nbsp;
something. And we always are waiting for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.560
hoping for confirmation of more details and just&nbsp;
something important to keep in mind when there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.800
assertions made in the fog of war, sometimes&nbsp;
the truth ends up being slightly different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.640
and that is certainly what Russia is hoping for&nbsp;
because of an absolutely disastrous headline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:40.560
60 People Killed After Bomb Hits School.&nbsp;
Vladimir Zelensky, the Ukrainian president,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:47.920
says this is a BBC report. Around 60 people were&nbsp;
killed after a bomb hit a school in east Ukraine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:55.120
says President Zelensky. Earlier, the governor&nbsp;
of the Luhansk region, Sergey Heidi, said 90&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:02.000
people had been sheltering in the building and&nbsp;
30 were rescued. Mr. Heidi said a Russian plane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.320
dropped the bomb on Saturday. Russia has not&nbsp;
commented. Luhansk has seen fierce combat as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.680
Russian troops and separatist fighters seek to&nbsp;
surround government forces. Much of the region&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.240
has been under the control of Russia backed&nbsp;
separatists for the past eight years. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:26.400
that detail is much of what's being used to say.&nbsp;
Russia would never do this. That's a region there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:32.000
separatist fighters have been in for so long. But&nbsp;
if we've learned one thing in the last few weeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.400
it's even things that lots of people say Russia&nbsp;
would never do. Then Russia does. And though and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:46.000
so I don't think we can go by that at all. We&nbsp;
also are waiting sort of anxiously to figure out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.240
what is it that might happen on Russia's so-called&nbsp;
victory day today, May 9th. And by the time that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:58.080
today's episode goes live, you may know more about&nbsp;
this than we know right now. An NBC News article&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:03.040
asks, What does Putin have planned on Russia's&nbsp;
victory day? Experts say that after two months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.960
of sordid, thwarted offensives, Putin is left&nbsp;
with limited options from an all out mobilization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.480
to simply declaring victory in the Eastern&nbsp;
Donbas region. Now, that's an interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.360
idea that's being brought up, which is&nbsp;
we don't know Putin's emotional state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.360
We don't know. Again, increasingly more and more&nbsp;
reports about Putin's ill health. We don't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:33.120
whether he is sort of in some kind of unhinged&nbsp;
last attempt at reconstructing the Soviet Union&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.160
in some kind of idealized way. We just don't&nbsp;
know what he is capable of and interested in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:46.640
But one idea that would be a face saving idea,&nbsp;
absent a victory so far when it comes to Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:52.800
at large, would be to say, hey, you know&nbsp;
what? We did it in the sense that we've now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.960
really solidified control of the Eastern&nbsp;
Donbass region. And even though we didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:05.280
take Kiev and some other places further&nbsp;
into Ukraine. Pointing west from Russia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:11.920
really this was the goal. And we did it and we&nbsp;
won. We took the Donbas region and of course it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.600
wouldn't be completely true, but it would at least&nbsp;
be more true. Then they took all of Ukraine, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:24.000
certainly Russia has not done. So that would be a&nbsp;
kind of face saving way for Putin maybe to start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.680
kind of backing up. But again, we just don't know.&nbsp;
A few other interesting notes from the article,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:35.520
which says Monday is shaping up to be a pivotal&nbsp;
day for Ukraine. Known as Victory Day in Russia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:41.920
May 9th is a national holiday commemorating the&nbsp;
Soviet Union's defeat of Nazi Germany in World War&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.160
Two, typically marked by an elaborate&nbsp;
military parade in Moscow's Red Square,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:52.560
surveyed by senior Kremlin officials. So a little&nbsp;
North Korea like. Yes, for sure. Western officials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.840
have voiced concerns that Putin will use the&nbsp;
occasion to officially declare war on Ukraine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:04.160
which Russia invaded in February. Experts say that&nbsp;
after more than two months of thwarted offensives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:10.000
Putin is left with limited options. As I said,&nbsp;
an all out mobilization. Or simply declaring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.720
victory in the Eastern Donbas region. Now,&nbsp;
on the declare war thing, we talked a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:21.360
bit about declare a war last week during a live&nbsp;
stream. As this article restates, Putin spokesman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:29.120
Dmitry Peskov denied that a war declaration was&nbsp;
imminent, insisting the invasion remained a,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:35.600
quote, special military operation. That may be&nbsp;
a nominal difference. As the article points out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:42.960
Since Russia has mobilized air, ground and&nbsp;
naval forces across vast areas of Ukraine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:49.920
But declaring war would allow Putin to call up&nbsp;
additional army reservists and more people and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:55.840
could prolong this for a certainly months,&nbsp;
if not years. So at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.440
we don't know what is coming. In the next 24&nbsp;
hours. By the time today's episode is out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:06.800
you may know more than I know right now, and we'll&nbsp;
follow up on that tomorrow. But no matter what I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:15.120
mean, in the best case where Putin says we won in&nbsp;
the sense that we got done, boss, there are going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:22.320
to be hostilities months or years for sure.&nbsp;
And what this means for the people of Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:27.360
can't possibly be particularly good. So we're&nbsp;
going to make an effort this week to make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.840
we stay on this story. There have been so many&nbsp;
other things that have happened in the last month.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:39.840
At the same time as there has been a sort of a&nbsp;
continued steady level of hostilities in Ukraine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:46.480
which often when things become normalized, like,&nbsp;
for example, kids dying of hunger every day all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:53.200
over the world, it becomes less of a corporate&nbsp;
news grab because corporate news stories tend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:57.360
to have a nice clean beginning, beginning, middle&nbsp;
and end. And if we just remain in the middle for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.920
a long time, sort of like happened with COVID,&nbsp;
as I said, happens with hunger around the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.440
it starts to come out of the news and that's&nbsp;
